  {
    "title": "HRA Investigation Exposes How Digital Matchmaking Platforms Facilitate Child Marriage in Iran",
    "link": "https://www.en-hrana.org/hra-investigation-exposes-how-digital-matchmaking-platforms-facilitate-child-marriage-in-iran/",
    "pubDate": "2026-10-08T13:34:59.000Z",
    "content": "<p><strong>HRANA News Agency – </strong>A new investigation by Human Rights Activists (HRA) documents how Iran’s “Adam and Eve” matchmaking platform allows minors to be presented as prospective spouses, while operating within a broader system of state licensing, promotion, financial incentives, and institutional support. The report also examines the role of international technology companies—including Google and Meta—in distributing and promoting services that may expose children to marriage, exploitation, and other forms of harm.</p>\n<p>Human Rights Activists (HRA) has published a new investigative report, <em>Child Marriage in the Digital Age</em>, examining how digital matchmaking services in Iran are creating new pathways through which child marriage can be facilitated and normalized.</p>",
    "snippet": "HRANA News Agency – A new investigation by Human Rights Activists (HRA) documents how Iran’s “Adam and Eve” matchmaking platform allows minors to be presented as prospective spouses, while operating",
