  {
    "title": "Hundreds of Cases Opened and Indictments Issued in Connection with Two Recent Wars",
    "link": "https://www.en-hrana.org/hundreds-of-cases-opened-and-indictments-issued-in-connection-with-two-recent-wars/",
    "pubDate": "2026-10-07T14:45:59.000Z",
    "content": "<p>According to HRANA, citing Mizan, Judiciary spokesperson Seyed Ali Kazemi said during a press conference addressing the latest status of cases related to what he described as “actions against the country’s security and national interests” that 476 cases have so far been opened in connection with the two recent wars.</p>\n<p>Kazemi added that proceedings in these cases are ongoing in prosecutors’ offices and courts, and that additional cases are being opened as new complaints are filed.</p>\n<p>He continued: “So far, 163 indictments have also been issued in connection with these two wars.” In another part of his remarks, addressing cases involving allegations of collaboration with Israel and hostile countries, Kazemi said: “In this regard, 250 cases have been opened, involving 1,895 defendants.”</p>\n<p>According to Kazemi, 94 of the defendants are media workers, while 1,801 are private individuals. The Judiciary spokesperson also announced that 70 indictments have so far been issued in connection with these individuals.</p>",
